    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70a74fa3_1bbf2fd3",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2099,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-14T07:58:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we guarantee that this interface will fire one callback for every call within a bounded time? Or can it happen for some reason (e.g., entitlement app crashes, network not available, etc) that a callback doesn\u0027t happen?\n\nWithout such a guarantee, I don\u0027t think it\u0027s acceptable to provide an interface of this form, because a caller will never know which of its outstanding requests triggered a given response.\n\nIf we can\u0027t provide such a guarantee, then we should return some form of error if a duplicate ResultReceiver is passed in (assuming we can tell), or find another way to avoid this confusion.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2099,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 2099,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "fa8edc59e6a98b39862b2e39fd964e9cfc4de33e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12699827_61d6b419",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2099,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080048
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-14T22:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Like I said in the last round of comments, the only case not handled correctly right now with multiple callbacks is if the entitlement app crashes. You\u0027re right that we should add a timeout to TetherService, but I\u0027d like to keep that separate from this CL because it\u0027s an issue even for the startTethering API right now. I\u0027ve filed a bug and cc\u0027d you and I intend to get a fix for that out to you shortly. Is it ok if we don\u0027t block this CL on that, though?",
      "parentUuid": "70a74fa3_1bbf2fd3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2099,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 2099,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "fa8edc59e6a98b39862b2e39fd964e9cfc4de33e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9fde062_8a383ed4",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 3105,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-14T07:58:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just realized this only checks ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE. I don\u0027t think it\u0027s appropriate, because:\n\n1. Starting tethering is a privileged information (regular\n   apps can\u0027t do it at all), and there\u0027s no point allowing\n   an app to call this method if it can\u0027t do tethering\n   anyway.\n2. If the provisioning check brings up cell data, that can\n   cause mobile data traffic at a time when the app itself\n   might not be able to cause such traffic.\n3. API guidelines require that @SystemApi methods are guarded\n   by permissions that regular apps cannot have.\n\nIs there a reason this can\u0027t use enforceTetherChangePermission?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3105,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 3105,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "fa8edc59e6a98b39862b2e39fd964e9cfc4de33e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
