    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dccc9dcf_f269a1a3",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 417,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-14T07:58:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this work on O even if you turn off mobile data always on? I suspect it might not.\n\nEven if it does, this seems a bit baroque. We\u0027re being called by ConnectivityService, from where it\u0027s trivial to determine whether the device has an active cell data connection or not.\n\nA simple way to do this in ConnectivityService would be:\n\n    @Override\n    public void runTetherProvisioningCheck(int type, ResultReceiver receiver) {\n        enforceTetherChangePermission();\n        mHandler.sendMessage(mHandler.obtainMessage(EVENT_RUN_TETHER_PROVISION_CHECK, type, 0, receiver));\n    }\n\n...\n\n    private boolean hasMobileInternetConnection() {\n        for (NetworkAgentInfo nai : mNetworkAgentInfos.values()) {\n            if (nai.networkCapabilities.hasCapability(NET_CAPABILITY_INTERNET) \u0026\u0026\n                    nai.networkCapabilities.hasTransport (TRANSPORT_CELLULAR)) {\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n...\n\n    case EVENT_RUN_TETHER_PROVISION_CHECK: {\n        \n        runTetherProvisioningCheck(msg.arg1, receiver, hasMobileInternetConnection());\n    }",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 371,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 417,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "fa8edc59e6a98b39862b2e39fd964e9cfc4de33e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba4504e8_9602c083",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 417,
      "author": {
        "id": 1080048
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-04-14T22:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your suggestion looks much cleaner! Is it good enough to tell whether there\u0027s sufficient connection strength to make the request? If the user is in a subway or anywhere else where there\u0027s no service at all, does this function still return true?",
      "parentUuid": "dccc9dcf_f269a1a3",
      "range": {
